    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d709">

                <pb facs="1014" n="1522" sameAs="frus:frus1948v05p2/pg1522"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Palestine/10–2048: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the United States
                        Delegation at Paris</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret   us urgent</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-10-27T18:00:00-05:00">October 27, 1948—6
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Gadel 337. In our opinion, US introduction and/or sponsorship text providing for
                    scale of contributions (Delga 494 Oct. 26<anchor n="1" xml:id="d709-f1"/>)
                    involves a US commitment which would make prior consultation Congressional
                    leaders essential. Such consultation not practicable at present, and would
                    necessitate further and unfortunate postponement Committee Three discussion.</p>
                <p>Regardless of means presentation appeal, we believe we can expect little tangible
                    assistance from any states except US, UK, Arabs, and possibly dominions.
                    Therefore, since bulk of contributions under either proposal will come from same
                    sources, we much prefer UK <pb facs="1015" n="1523" xml:id="pg1523"/>
                        draft,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d709-f2"/> embodying only moral obligation for
                    all Members, rather than USDel proposal which involves specifying degree of
                    interest for every member. Dorr<anchor n="3" xml:id="d709-f3"/> concurs
                    foregoing and view that fictitious budget more difficult present Congress.</p>
                <p>Re your numbered para 3, introduction resolution along US lines would almost
                    certainly open up undesirable and prolonged political debate concerning question
                    responsibility for creation refugee problem.</p>
                <p>Moreover Committee 3 action might be prejudiced if draft scale contributions not
                    submitted with draft resolution. Determination scale would involve time
                    consuming and difficult negotiations.</p>
                <p>Dept. feels that UK proposal (Delga 423, Oct 20 par <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >b</hi>) would be more likely win Committee 3 support.<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d709-f4"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d709-f1" n="1" xml:id="d709-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d709-f2" n="2" xml:id="d709-f2-content">
                <p>As transmitted in telegram Delga 423, October 20, 11 p. m., from Paris, not
                    printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d709-f3" n="3" xml:id="d709-f3-content">
                <p>Goldthwaite H. Dorr of the Executive Secretariat.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d709-f4" n="4" xml:id="d709-f4-content">
                <p>The joint resolution was actually sponsored, on October 29, by Belgium and the
                    Netherlands, as well as by the United Kingdom and the United States; for text,
                    see United Nations, <hi rendition="#italic">Official Records of the Third
                        Session of the General Assembly, Part I, Third Committee, Annexes,
                    1948</hi>, p. 51.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
